 as a resource to nurture the commons","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-052578","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This paper explores possibilities and challenges of introducing the collaborative web-based, wiki-inspired tool Pycipedia in Swedish municipalities. Pycipedia is designed to support social workers that work with assisting parents with cognitive impairments. Pycipedia is co-designed with social workers and digitalize some of their workflows, enabling new ways of working and allow professional collaboration across municipalities. Pycipedia has now been used ‘live’ for two and a half years with users in six municipalities. This paper present and discuss observations and reflections coming from running such a long-term ‘live’ evaluation of a tool that digitalize parts of an existing practice. Our findings deal with the effects of moving social care practices online, the inherent fragility of commitment over time, and the social worker as knowledge creators and sharers. An important perspective is the long-term implementation of our tool in the social workers’ everyday practice.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grönvall, Erik","Lundberg, Stefan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382947"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","LCO Prime AB"],"keyword":["Collaborative Tools","Digitalization","Municipal Implementation","Pycipedia","Social work"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing for offline and online social work technology mediated collaborative practices in and between municipalities","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86875891/ECCE2022_CameraReady_29062022.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382947","identifier":[{"id":"85139924133","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7121c6ab-8e79-42e1-a43b-3b967072e0dc"],"keyword":["Collaborative Tools","Digitalization","Municipal Implementation","Pycipedia","Social Work"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F84F16B9E5FA1519D58C4460D9405F73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86875891/ECCE2022_CameraReady_29062022.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lco prime ab","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"LCO Prime AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"lundbergpau","last":"Lundberg","name":"Lundberg, Stefan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3552327.3552334","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"ECCE 2022","title":"European conference on cognitive ergonomics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139924133"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7121c6ab-8e79-42e1-a43b-3b967072e0dc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing for offline and online social work: Technology-mediated collaborative practices in and between municipalities","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382947","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Commons traditionally refer to shared natural resources that are at risk of being depleted or even destroyed. The rules established by commoners offer a way to manage such scarce resources. Through a series of projects on national eHealth patient health records, we have identified another type of shared resources – semantic resources – that would benefit from commons-based governance. Semantic resources are standardised definitions of data that ensure a common understanding of data during processes of data sharing between different actors and systems. In this paper, we first use commons as a lens to explore shared semantic resources and the governance challenges associated with them (e.g. lack of cross-cutting support across many projects). This leads to a better understanding of (1) shared semantic resources as global commons, (2) the relationship between the global and local levels of semantic resource governance and, by observing traces of commoning at the local level, (3) the role of commoning as a crucial concept in the context of semantic interoperability. Second, we introduce the notion of semantic commons to address the governance problems of semantic resources that needs to be continuous and sustainable. In addition, we also contribute to the commons literature by proposing a new area of research for commons scholars. We identify semantic resources in healthcare as an interesting and important type of resource that offers a new perspective on the dynamics of the relationship between global and local commons. We also identify a central role for commoning in healthcare in general as well as in the governance of semantic resources there.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bestek, Mate","Grönvall, Erik","Saad-Sulonen, Joanna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382970"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Commoning","Healthcare","Semantic Interoperability","local commons","semantic resources governance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"commoning semantic interoperability in healthcare","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5334/ijc.1157","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382970","identifier":[{"id":"85135487629","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-730d9abe-bf5e-4d05-b813-a5c514c8ac5a"],"keyword":["commoning","healthcare","local commons","semantic interoperability","semantic resources governance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-54ADC22B74D4AF59C52347C45BCF4BDD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5334/ijc.1157","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mate","key":"bestekpau","last":"Bestek","name":"Bestek, Mate","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanna","key":"saadsulonenpau","last":"Saad-Sulonen","name":"Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5334/ijc.1157","issn":["18750281"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of the Commons","pages":"225-242","paperid":"16","publisher":"Ubiquity Press","status":"p","title":"International Journal of the Commons","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135487629"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-730d9abe-bf5e-4d05-b813-a5c514c8ac5a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Commoning semantic interoperability in healthcare","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382970","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Previous Participatory design (PD) and HCI work have discussed the outcomes of research and design projects, their processes, technology innovations, methods, and users. Researchers have also examined the phases of collaborative research projects, including the ‘before’, ‘during’ and ‘after’ stages. There are however substantially more papers describing aspects of participation and collaboration in the during and after stages of a design research project compared with papers discussing collaborative activities before the formal project starts, during the pre-project activities where a project is negotiated, and its finances secured. This paper uses two municipal co-design research projects to explore participatory and collaborative processes as they unfolded before the actual projects started. By mainly considering the before-stage of these projects, this paper sheds light on a less studied aspect of many co-design projects, and research projects in general – how they came into being and the role of participation in designing the project-to-be.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grönvall, Erik","Lundberg, Stefan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383678"],"event":{"acronym":"OzCHI","title":"Conference of the Australian Computer-Human Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","LCO Prime AB"],"keyword":["Co design","Collaborative Processes","Human Computer Interaction","Participatory Design","Pre Project Activities"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring participatory pre project processes making research work in municipality organizations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90382681/OzCHI2022_CameraReady_Final_01092022_preTAPS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383678","ids":["itu-a55d7e13-b395-4c8c-8c3c-5c391f2e8225"],"keyword":["Co-Design","Collaborative Processes","Human-Computer Interaction","Participatory Design","Pre-Project Activities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2830720E1055FBC4FC8F431B4E0D2DC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90382681/OzCHI2022_CameraReady_Final_01092022_preTAPS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ozchi.org/2022/static/papers/paper1073.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lco prime ab","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"LCO Prime AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"lundbergpau","last":"Lundberg","name":"Lundberg, Stefan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"OzCHI 2022: the 34th Annual Conference of the Australian Computer-Human Interaction Special Group"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a55d7e13-b395-4c8c-8c3c-5c391f2e8225"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring participatory pre-project processes: Making research work in municipality organizations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383678","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this case study we take a Nordic perspective on the tension between increased digitalisation of public services and the insufficient support for citizens with limited digital literacy. Volunteer-based IT helpdesk services in public libraries have emerged as an attempt to address this tension. Drawing on examples of volunteering in public library-based IT helpdesk services in two Nordic countries, this paper considers the IT helpdesks as quasi-public services. Based on interviews, observations and workshops, we explore: the work of IT helpdesk volunteers, the characteristics of helpdesk services offered, and the implications of these services being offered by volunteers. The services offered are of acceptable quality to the users while the ambiguity and lack of institutional support is making the service fragile. In spite of the challenges of the quasi-public IT helpdesk service we also note how it offers a potential platform for the co-design and support of new public services.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christensen, Camilla Vesterberg","Ehrenberg, Nils","Messeter, Jörn","Grönvall, Erik","Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","Keinonen, Turkka"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381392"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Co design","Digital literacy","Digitalization","IT Helpdesk","Nordic Perspective","Public libraries","Public services","Quasi Public Services","Service quality","Volunteering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"volunteer based it helpdesks as ambiguous quasi public services a case study from two nordic countries","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90345557/NordiCHI_TAPS_formatted_FINAL.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381392","ids":["itu-09376cbc-40c9-4f5a-a6cb-13bc190d3fe9"],"keyword":["Co-Design","Digital Literacy","Digitalization","IT Helpdesk","Nordic Perspective","Public Libraries","Public Services","Quasi-Public Services","Service Quality","Volunteering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B387F5B446022CB7A04A445C5CCF5370"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90345557/NordiCHI_TAPS_formatted_FINAL.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla Vesterberg","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"42d8cef2-2fa9-4545-b4f4-a44dadf4934f","name":"Christensen, Camilla Vesterberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils","key":"ehrenbergpau","last":"Ehrenberg","name":"Ehrenberg, Nils","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jörn","key":"christianssonpau","last":"Christiansson","locid":"a4c1604d-b01f-46ef-baf3-74d2a8046d6b","name":"Messeter, Jörn","name_org":"Christiansson, Jörn","orcid":"0000-0002-2181-149X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanna","key":"saadsulonenpau","last":"Saad-Sulonen","name":"Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Turkka","key":"keinonenpau","last":"Keinonen","name":"Keinonen, Turkka","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"1-12","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '22: Nordic Human-Computer Interaction Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-09376cbc-40c9-4f5a-a6cb-13bc190d3fe9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Volunteer-based IT Helpdesks as Ambiguous Quasi-Public Services : A Case Study from Two Nordic Countries","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381392","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we compare two cases of collaboration within healthcare in two European countries, Denmark and France respectively. In each of these two cases, we conducted a design case study, and we found that collaboration is ad hoc, temporary, and shifting with regards to collaborators, aims, and processes. We argue for the relevance of knotworking and its analytic potential for investigating the kind of collaborative work we observed. We also argue that our two cases present a higher complexity level than how knotworking has previously been described in the literature. We describe complex knotworking as having three characteristics: 1) collaboration happens between a dynamic number of actors (who are usually loosely connected), 2) collaboration happens in episodes, and 3) cooperative work arrangements are constantly negotiated. Using the concept of complex knotworking for a comparative analysis of our two design solutions, we outline generic design guidelines for developing computer support to manage complex knotworking situations.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Amsha, Khuloud Abou","Bossen, Claus","Grönvall, Erik","Lewkowicz, Myriam"],"cuid":["S02-083.41-024288"],"event":{"acronym":"CSCW","title":"ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Amsha, Khuloud Abou"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Troyes University of Technology","Universite de Technologie de Troyes"],"keyword":["Ad hoc collaboration","CSCW","Design guidelines","Healthcare","Knotworking"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computer supported knotworking design guidelines based on two case studies from the healthcare domain in europe","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86117611/cscw20d_sub2460_cam_i26_1_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-083.41-024288","identifier":[{"id":"85130621343","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9ecfc47e-3a81-4316-bcee-6afb9ed9f582","itu-ff07f4c3-ab0b-423e-8a3d-0c1731393b95"],"keyword":["CSCW","ad-hoc collaboration","design guidelines","healthcare","knotworking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D1C1B3207A25E7A71882B98C96811E97"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86117611/cscw20d_sub2460_cam_i26_1_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"universite de technologie de troyes","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universite de Technologie de Troyes","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"troyes university of technology","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Troyes University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Information Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Khuloud Abou","key":"amshapau","last":"Amsha","name":"Amsha, Khuloud Abou","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Khuloud","key":"abouamshapau","last":"Abou Amsha","name":"Abou Amsha, Khuloud","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"bossenpau","last":"Bossen","locid":"f989b328-ea2e-4b6f-b6c5-90d61465d153","name":"Bossen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-3698-0675","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Myriam","key":"lewkowiczpau","last":"Lewkowicz","name":"Lewkowicz, Myriam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3449199","issn":["25730142"],"issue":"1","journal":"Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction","paperid":"125","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130621343"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9ecfc47e-3a81-4316-bcee-6afb9ed9f582","itu-ff07f4c3-ab0b-423e-8a3d-0c1731393b95"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computer-Supported Knotworking: Design Guidelines Based on Two Case Studies from the Healthcare Domain in Europe","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.41-024288","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we address the lack of user involvement in the development of public e-services. Based on related literature, we present a contextualization of civic participation and participatory design (in its historical Scandinavian approach) in relation to public e-service innovation. We describe an upcoming project collaborating with public libraries in three Nordic countries, and put forward some open questions about possible directions for the planned project work. Through this paper and work we contribute to the development of more fine-grained and refined concepts related to spaces of innovation. We also outline the potential role of participatory design in and for the public sector.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Messeter, Jörn","Grönvall, Erik","Saad-Sulonen, Joanna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383416"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Civic participation","Innovation in the Public Sector","Participatory Design","Public e services","User involvement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"setting the stage for the participatory design of public e services public libraries as hosts of civic innovation centres","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383416","ids":["itu-921ad1fd-638a-4aac-b73e-f27aacbc43ce"],"keyword":["Civic participation","Innovation in the public sector","Participatory design","Public e-services","User involvement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3144458D586650EF54E97E5330698BE9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jörn","key":"christianssonpau","last":"Christiansson","locid":"a4c1604d-b01f-46ef-baf3-74d2a8046d6b","name":"Messeter, Jörn","name_org":"Christiansson, Jörn","orcid":"0000-0002-2181-149X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanna","key":"saadsulonenpau","last":"Saad-Sulonen","name":"Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-921ad1fd-638a-4aac-b73e-f27aacbc43ce"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Setting the stage for the participatory design of public e-services: public libraries as hosts of Civic Innovation Centres.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383416","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The Covid-19 pandemic struck the world in spring 2019 and affected most people in the world. One group that suffered the most was older adults and others ‘weak’ citizens. In Sweden where the reported-on study was situated, especially people living in nursing homes and other care facilities suffered immensely, especially in the early stages of the pandemic. In this paper we report on perspectives and lessons learned from a survey compiled by 13 care managers in eleven Swedish municipalities followed by a workshop with ten of these municipality health managers. Our study showcase how technology has been a valuable tool for these organizations during the pandemic. While Internet-cameras in some instances has been used in private homes to facilitate ‘remote monitoring’, many of our findings points to aspects of managing care – a less studied aspect within the Pervasive health community.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grönvall, Erik","Lundberg, Stefan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383376"],"event":{"acronym":"PervasiveHealth","title":"EAI International Conference on Pervasive Computing Technologies for Healthcare"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","LCO Prime AB"],"keyword":["COVID 19 pandemic","Nursing Homes","Older adults care","Pervasive health","Remote monitoring"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aspects of pervasive health and technology use in care organizations during the pandemic report from a municipality covid 000000000019 study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86353373/gronvall_MunPanWorkshop_toITU.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383376","ids":["itu-8f3b3a70-da98-4320-b0bf-4fa6c8d51e82"],"keyword":["Covid-19 pandemic","Nursing homes","Older adults care","Pervasive health","Remote monitoring"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-181459C9F044FAB111CD6BF9C6EE8455"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86353373/gronvall_MunPanWorkshop_toITU.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lco prime ab","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"LCO Prime AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"lundbergpau","last":"Lundberg","name":"Lundberg, Stefan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"1-10","publisher":"European Alliance for Innovation","status":"p","title":"EAI PervasiveHealth 2021 - 15th EAI International Conference on Pervasive Computing Technologies for Healthcare"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8f3b3a70-da98-4320-b0bf-4fa6c8d51e82"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Aspects of pervasive health and technology use in care organizations during the pandemic: Report from a municipality Covid-19 study","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383376","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The rise of Big Data and data science has prompted a focus on data as an essential component of making and innovating data-based services. Traditionally, however, digital data has not been object to co-design as have other physical or functional dimensions of IT application design. This is problematic, because it hinders domain experts who are not IT professionals from taking part in the discussions and design of the data-based services they use and provide. We argue that to address this challenge, it is necessary to empower such domain experts to be able to consider data as an object of design, so they may contribute their expertise to the design of data-based services and their underlying data structures. This paper describes how data may be foregrounded as an explicit element of design that support domain experts’ understanding of data as something that can be designed. We present a detailed interaction analysis of video recordings of three collaborative design workshops, in which we propose a form of data notation and two data representations. We find that data may become an object of design for domain experts when tangible and flexible representations of data are used. Based on our findings, we discuss five lessons learned for foregrounding data in co-design. Together, these provide practical insights for future work.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Seidelin, Cathrine","Dittrich, Yvonne","Grönvall, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382975"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Co design","Data","Data as an object of design","Data as input for design","Participatory Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"foregrounding data in co design an exploration of how data may become an object of design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhcs.2020.102505","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382975","identifier":[{"id":"85087910706","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7368138d-33e4-4132-84c5-a86f61b50c2b"],"keyword":["Co-design","Data","Data as an object of design","Data as input for design","Participatory design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2EB1CECEDFC15F08DCB44F3E2972CF11"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhcs.2020.102505","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85444034/20200703_ForegroundingData_JournalPreProof.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cathrine","key":"seidelinpau","last":"Seidelin","name":"Seidelin, Cathrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhcs.2020.102505","issn":["10715819","10959300"],"issn_org":["10715819"],"journal":"International Journal of Human-Computer Studies","pages":"1-18","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Human-Computer Studies","volume":"143"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087910706"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7368138d-33e4-4132-84c5-a86f61b50c2b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Foregrounding data in co-design – An exploration of how data may become an object of design","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382975","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Data leakage and privacy are well known but abstract terms for most people. To grant people a real-time and on-body experience of data leakage as it happens, we constructed CreepyLeaks. CreepyLeaks turns data leakage into a visceral embodied experience that augments visual information about what data are leaked, where and via which application. Conducting evaluations of CreepyLeaks we learned the value of the public demonstrations over individual encounters with privacy technologies. Rather than inspiring the audience to think positively about a design or functionality, the demo became an opportunity to develop collective ideas of concepts and problems that are difficult to grasp individually. By conducting privacy technology demos in public and semi-public events, we demonstrate how demos can create conditions for participatory speculation – a practice involving a confluence of human and non-human actors in speculative experiences, acknowledging the politics inherent in technology design and collectively considering possible futures.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Shklovski, Irina","Grönvall, Erik"],"cuid":["S02-094.83-038270"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","end":"2020-10-29","place":"Tallinn, ee","start":"2020-10-25","title":"11th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction: Shaping Experiences, Shaping Society","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Creepy","DEMO","Data leakage","Demonstration","Participatory speculation","Privacy","Speculative experiences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"creepyleaks participatory speculation through demos","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3419249.3420168","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-094.83-038270","identifier":[{"id":"85095827905","type":"scopus"},{"id":"85123043148","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1f2c63ba-4ac0-45d7-a55e-8b0e7e84a564","ku-bcb1b756-ed43-4a3a-8032-df18afd388ba"],"keyword":["Creepy","Data leakage","Demo","Demonstration","Participatory speculation","Privacy","Speculative experiences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BE349B76B4D08CF6C939986263CD89F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85460481/nordichi20_107.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3419249.3420168","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centred Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Irina","key":"shklovskipau","last":"Shklovski","locid":"e5067505-4088-4c76-b398-aedd455ed164","name":"Shklovski, Irina","orcid":"0000-0003-1874-0958","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3419249.3420168","eisbn":["9781450375795"],"pages":"1-12","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '20: Proceedings of the 11th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction: Shaping Experiences, Shaping Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123043148"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1f2c63ba-4ac0-45d7-a55e-8b0e7e84a564","ku-bcb1b756-ed43-4a3a-8032-df18afd388ba"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"CreepyLeaks : Participatory Speculation Through Demos","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.83-038270","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Today, organizations have to deal with multiple heterogeneous data sources from different systems and platforms to maintain and develop their services. Therefore, there is a need for tools to support organizations to determine what data sources can advance and innovate their services. This paper reports on how we addressed this need by designing and implementing two design tools – the Data Sphere and the Data Experiment Template – to support domain experts’ exploration with different data sources which they selected themselves. We find that (1) domain experts’ exploration of data sources make the cross-organizational dependency of data and data work visible; (2) the value of co-design becomes evident to address this dependency; and by that, (3) the data became ‘design things’, that means data are object of design that at the same time create a space for members of the organization to together explore how to use data to innovate their services.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Seidelin, Cathrine","Dittrich, Yvonne","Grönvall, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383799"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Co design","Data Experiments","Data Sphere","Data work","Design Things","Organization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co designing data experiments domain experts exploration and experimentation with self selected data sources","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85460420/CoDesigningDataExperiments.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383799","identifier":[{"id":"85123041762","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ae489b73-54d7-4ecc-be55-c1428caddb24"],"keyword":["Co-design","Data Experiments","Data Sphere","Data Work","Design Things","Organization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25A24E8C19BC3BF201AD4CE7959745FF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85460420/CoDesigningDataExperiments.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cathrine","key":"seidelinpau","last":"Seidelin","name":"Seidelin, Cathrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3419249.3420152","eisbn":["9781450375795"],"pages":"1-11","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '20: Proceedings of the 11th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction: Shaping Experiences, Shaping Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123041762"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ae489b73-54d7-4ecc-be55-c1428caddb24"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Co-designing Data Experiments: Domain Experts’ Exploration and Experimentation with self-selected Data Sources","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383799","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PYCIPEDIA is a web-based collaborative tool for social workers that support parents with intellectual disabilities taking care of their small children. These particular social workers have been certified in providing parenting-skills training and support for parents with intellectual disabilities or with learning difficulties. As only a relatively small number of social workers are certified in providing the relevant support, there may be few colleagues to discuss with and learn from, even in larger municipalities with many social workers. To support social workers in providing the best possible support, the web-based collaborative tool PYCIPEDIA has been co-designed with social workers from two Swedish municipalities. The tool allows social workers to log in, and independent from what municipality they work in, create, browse, edit and share material (e.g. text, images and video) that can support the parents. They can discuss cases, rate online material, and access a forum.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grönvall, Erik","Lundberg, Stefan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381650"],"event":{"acronym":"CSCW","title":"ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Collaborative tool","Intellectual disabilities","Parenting skills training","Social workers","Web based platform"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pycipedia supporting local and remote collaboration between social workers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84838727/cscw2019_poster_PYC_FINAL_TO_ITU.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381650","identifier":[{"id":"85076096561","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1987fdc0-5910-40ad-bd33-0fa82a67810a"],"keyword":["Collaborative tool","Intellectual disabilities","Parenting-skills training","Social workers","Web-based platform"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7ACAF6855D6A24A1EC290049167BB859"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84838727/cscw2019_poster_PYC_FINAL_TO_ITU.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"lundbergpau","last":"Lundberg","name":"Lundberg, Stefan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3311957.3359499","pages":"195-200","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"CSCW '19 Conference Companion Publication of the 2019 on Computer Supported Cooperative Work and Social Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076096561"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1987fdc0-5910-40ad-bd33-0fa82a67810a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"PYCIPEDIA: Supporting Local and Remote Collaboration between Social Workers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381650","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The term Human-Data Interaction (HDI) conceptualizes the growing importance of understanding how people need and desire to use and interact with data. Previous HDI cases have mainly focused on the interface between personal health data and the healthcare sector. This paper argues that it is relevant to consider HDI at an organisational level and examines how HDI can look in such a context, where data and data maintenance are core assets and activities. We report on initial findings of a study of a knowledge-broker organisation, where we follow how data are produced, shared, and maintained in a cross-organisational context. We discuss similarities and differences of HDI around personal health data and cross-organisational data maintenance. We propose to extend the notion of HDI to include the complexity of cross-organisational data work.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Seidelin, Cathrine","Dittrich, Yvonne","Grönvall, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384322"],"event":{"acronym":"HCI","title":"International BCS Human Computer Interaction Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross Organisational Data","Data Maintenance","Data Usage Practices","Human data interaction","Knowledge Brokerage"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data work in a knowledge broker organization how cross organizational data maintenance shapes human data interactions","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14236/ewic/HCI2018.14","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384322","identifier":[{"id":"85058124017","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d0464844-a319-43e4-9351-03c58973ed7c"],"keyword":["Cross-Organisational Data","Data Maintenance","Data Usage Practices","Human-Data Interaction","Knowledge Brokerage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-04C615381F0628363497AECA0D82A527"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ewic.bcs.org/content/conWebDoc/59990","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14236/ewic/HCI2018.14","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83317750/BHCI_2018_paper_48.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cathrine","key":"seidelinpau","last":"Seidelin","name":"Seidelin, Cathrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.14236/ewic/hci2018.14","isbn":["N/A"],"pages":"1-12","place":"Belfast, Northern Ireland","publisher":"BCS Learning and Development Ltd","status":"p","title":"British Human Computer Interaction Conference 2018"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058124017"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University