{"abstract":"Organisations are looking for new service offers through innovative use of data, often through a Service Design approach. However, current Service Design tools conceal technological aspects of service development like data and datasets. Data can support the design of future services but is often not represented or rendered as a readily workable design material. This paper reports on an early qualitative study of the tools used to work with data and analytics in a medium-sized organisation. The findings identify the current representations of data and data analytics used in the case organisation. We discuss to which extend the available representations of data and data analytics support data-driven service innovation. A comparison of our findings and current Service Design representations show that Service Design lack to represent data as design material. We propose the notion of expansiveness as a criterion to evaluate future data representations for data-driven Service Design.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Seidelin, Cathrine","Dittrich, Yvonne","Grönvall, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381459"],"event":{"acronym":"IRIS","title":"Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Big data","Design Artefacts","Service innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of a need for data representations in service design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82951845/Identification_of_a_need_for_data_representations_in_Service_Design_IRIS_2017_12.12.17_CS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381459","ids":["itu-0d049c3a-a9ea-4ce9-8aaf-e19495c97d3a"],"keyword":["Big Data","Design Artefacts","Service Innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CCF0DF6919D4BA4BD32F3567404A210F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82951845/Identification_of_a_need_for_data_representations_in_Service_Design_IRIS_2017_12.12.17_CS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cathrine","key":"seidelinpau","last":"Seidelin","name":"Seidelin, Cathrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18919863","23873353"],"issn_org":["18919863"],"issue":"10","journal":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","publisher":"Scandinavian Chapter of the Association for Information Systems (AIS) - Scandinavian IRIS","status":"p","title":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0d049c3a-a9ea-4ce9-8aaf-e19495c97d3a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Identification of a need for data representations in Service Design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381459","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The way the Computer Supported Cooperative work (CSCW) community talks about, defines and investigates ‘work’ has changed since the early workplace studies. In the current literature, work has been described as being distributed, cross-organizational and multi-actor dependent, volunteer-based, fleeting, opportunistic, inbetween and community-based. Collaborative work has also been examined in the formation of Publics, as Infrastructuring or as Knotworking. Work and collaborative work is indeed something that can be unforeseen by most or all of the involved actors. It can emerge and take place temporarily at the boundaries of established entities, and be independent of existing collaboration protocols. This workshop seeks to bring together researchers and practitioners who are interested in how we study and discuss very open-ended and emergent forms of collaboration, occurring in improvised, temporary communities of action, at the boundaries of established communities or organizations, to address issue that challenges current organization of work. The aim of the workshop is to open a space of reflection on relevant concepts, through the discussion of concrete examples and cases.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Abou Amsha, Khuloud","Grönvall, Erik","Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","Bossen, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381536"],"event":{"acronym":"C&T","title":"International Conference on Communities and Technologies"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","France"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations","Troyes University of Technology"],"keyword":["Computer Supported Cooperative Work","Cross organizational Collaboration","Distributed work","Emergent Collaboration","Temporary Communities"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"understanding and supporting emergent and temporary collaboration across and beyond community and organizational boundaries","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82388378/supporting_emergent_and_temporary_collaboration_Workshop_proposal_ITUversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381536","identifier":[{"id":"85025167191","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-11f79889-98e7-4973-a7f9-904197f9f2ba"],"keyword":["Computer Supported Cooperative Work","Cross-organizational Collaboration","Distributed Work","Emergent Collaboration","Temporary Communities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F99FCF203FCD9A1CDA47B9DF351A2AAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82388378/supporting_emergent_and_temporary_collaboration_Workshop_proposal_ITUversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"troyes university of technology","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Troyes University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Khuloud","key":"abouamshapau","last":"Abou Amsha","name":"Abou Amsha, Khuloud","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanna","key":"saadsulonenpau","last":"Saad-Sulonen","name":"Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"bossenpau","last":"Bossen","name":"Bossen, Claus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3083671.3083717","eisbn":["9781450348546"],"pages":"331-333","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"International Conference on Communities and Technologies","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 8th International Conference on Communities and Technologies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025167191"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-11f79889-98e7-4973-a7f9-904197f9f2ba"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Understanding and supporting emergent and temporary collaboration across and beyond community and organizational boundaries","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381536","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper stresses the need for more research in the field of Participatory Design (PD) and in particular into how to design Health Information Technology (HIT) together with care providers and -receivers in multicultural settings. We contribute to this research by describing a case study, the ‘Health-Cultures’ project, in which we designed HIT for the context of home care of older people with a migration background. The Health-Cultures project is located in the city of Genk, Belgium, which is known for its multicultural population, formed by three historical migration waves of people coming to work in the nowadays closed coal mines. Via a PD approach, we studied existing means of dialogue and designed HIT that both care receivers and care providers in Genk can use in their daily exchanges between cultures in home care contexts. In discussing relevant literature as well as the results of this study, we point to the need and the ways of taking spatio-historical aspects of a specific healthcare situation into account in the PD of HIT to support multicultural perspectives on healthcare.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Dreessen, Katrien","Huybrechts, Liesbeth","Grönvall, Erik","Hendriks, Niels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383893"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hasselt University","Social Spaces, LUCA School of Arts"],"keyword":["Health information technology","Home care","Migration Background","Multicultural Healthcare","Participatory Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infrastructuring multicultural healthcare information systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85011048681","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383893","identifier":[{"id":"85011048681","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b48f4596-578e-4e33-804d-c344f1f59d81"],"keyword":["Health Information Technology","Home Care","Migration Background","Multicultural Healthcare","Participatory Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BE52C57C45AE7A98F3C22738A156C82B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"be","key":"social spaces luca school of arts","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Social Spaces, LUCA School of Arts","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"hasselt university","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hasselt University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrien","key":"dreessenpau","last":"Dreessen","name":"Dreessen, Katrien","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Liesbeth","key":"huybrechtspau","last":"Huybrechts","name":"Huybrechts, Liesbeth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"hendrikspau","last":"Hendriks","name":"Hendriks, Niels","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3233/978-1-61499-740-5-30","eisbn":["9781614997405"],"isbn":["9781614997399"],"issn":["09269630"],"pages":"30-44","place":"Amsterdam","publisher":"IOS Press","series":"Studies in Health Technology and Informatics","status":"p","title":"Participatory Design and Health Information Technology","volume":"233"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85011014927"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b48f4596-578e-4e33-804d-c344f1f59d81"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infrastructuring Multicultural Healthcare Information Systems","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383893","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Later developments in community-based PD have put a focus on how societal challenges and technological possibilities call for new forms of participation and civic engagement. In particular, lack of resources promotes public engagement in social innovation, and highlights questions of how innovations developed in a local community can successfully 'travel' to other settings. In this full-day workshop, we take a hands-on approach in exploring how social innovations can 'travel' between different settings through a concrete design case. A digital platform co-designed with stakeholders in a municipality in Copenhagen and in two neighbourhood groups in Vienna is brought to the workshop. Representatives from the city of Aarhus will participate as local stakeholders to engage with workshop participants in a one-day 'designathon' to explore the challenges of appropriating this social innovation to the local setting of Aarhus. Participants will leave with concrete experiences from an exploration of how a particular social innovation can 'travel'; involving real stakeholders in co-design of solutions to the challenges at hand.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Messeter, Jörn","Grönvall, Erik","Malmborg, Lone","Fitzpatrick, Geraldine","Subasi, Özge","Brandt, Eva","Sønderlev Christensen, Martin","Raben, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382065"],"event":{"acronym":"PDC","end":"2016-08-19","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2016-08-15","title":"Participatory Design Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Vienna University of Technology"],"keyword":["Civic engagement","Social innovation","local appropriation","sharing community"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-AR