ecture","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Causing Commotion with a Shape-changing Bench : Experiencing Shape-Changing Interfaces in Use","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-088.20-741630","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Monitoring of health parameters in non-clinical settings is one strategy to address the increasingly aging population and age-related disabilities and diseases. However, challenges exist when introducing self-monitoring activities in people’s everyday life. An active lifestyle can challenge the appropriation of healthcare technologies and people with comorbidity may have diverse but co-existing monitoring needs. In this paper, we seek to understand home-based health monitoring practices to better design and integrate them into people’s everyday life. We perform an analysis of socio-technical complexities in home-based healthcare technologies through three case studies of self-monitoring: 1) pre-eclampsia (i.e. pregnancy poisoning), 2) heart conditions, and 3) preventive care. Through the analysis seven themes emerged (people, resources, places, routines, knowledge, control and motivation) that can facilitate the understanding of home-based healthcare activities. We present three modes of self-monitoring use and provide a set of design recommendations for future Ubicomp designs of home-based healthcare technology.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Grönvall, Erik","Verdezoto, Nervo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-129779"],"event":{"end":"2013-09-12","place":"Zurich, ch","start":"2013-09-08","title":"The 2013 ACM International Joint Conference on Pervasive and Ubiquitous Computing","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Case studies","Personal health management","Self monitoring","home based healthcare technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beyond self monitoring understanding non functional aspects of home based healthcare technology","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/55426724/ubi1515_gronvall.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-129779","identifier":[{"id":"84885224368","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-00e3d067-2fc5-475c-9d90-9c42c104a323"],"keyword":["Case Studies","Personal health management","Self-monitoring","home-based healthcare technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-299FCAA95520391ACAA31A03876CCE1B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2493432.2493495","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?doid=2493432.2493495","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/55426724/ubi1515_gronvall.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Participatory Information Technology","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"b600b501-1612-47fd-9286-f687efaefaf0","name":"Grönvall, Erik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nervo","key":"verdezotopau","last":"Verdezoto","locid":"ce629209-5619-4b43-88fb-b8fd03725adb","name":"Verdezoto, Nervo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Friedemann","key":"matternpedh","last":"Mattern","name":"Mattern, Friedemann","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Silvia","key":"santinipedh","last":"Santini","name":"Santini, Silvia","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2493432.2493495","isbn":["9781450322157"],"pages":"587-596","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2013 ACM Conference on Pervasive and Ubiquitous Computing, UbiComp '13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84885224368"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-00e3d067-2fc5-475c-9d90-9c42c104a323"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Beyond Self-Monitoring: Understanding Non-functional Aspects of Home-based Healthcare Technology","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-129779","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Several projects have shown that self-management of medication in private homes can be challenging. Many projects focused on specific illness-related approaches (e.g. diabetes) or practical issues such as how to handle medication while travelling. However, designing for everyday medication management involves more than just specific illness-related strategies and should take into account the broad set of activities conforming people’s everyday life. This study investigates how older adults manage their medication in everyday life. To inform the design of pervasive healthcare medication management systems (PHMMS), the study calls for attention to medication-specific particularities that account for: according to need medication, the heterogeneous care network, the substitute medication, the medication informational order, the shared responsibility and the adjustment of medication intake. These medication particularities can enhance the individual’s medication overview and support the understanding of medication intake in everyday life. The study also presents five design principles for future design of PHMMS.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Dalgaard, Lea Gulstav","Grönvall, Erik","Verdezoto, Nervo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-269664"],"event":{"acronym":"PervasiveHealth","end":"2013-05-08","place":"Venice, it","start":"2013-05-05","title":"International Conference on Pervasive Computing Technologies for Healthcare","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Medication management","Older adults","Personalized","Qualitative","Quantitative","User Centered Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accounting for medication particularities designing for everyday medication management","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/57006435/MedicationParticularitiesPervasiveHealth2013.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-269664","identifier":[{"id":"84883112744","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f5fb8d89-1705-4f20-a9b4-e56383f8bd0e"],"keyword":["Medication Management","Older Adults","Personalized","Qualitative","Quantitative","User Centered Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-6A1791F6561A45B57A7FC1B8B843465A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4108/pervasivehealth.2013.252058","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/57006435/MedicationParticularitiesPervasiveHealth2013.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/search/searchresult.jsp?queryText%3Dpervasivehealth+2013&refinements=4278559804&pageNumber=1&resultAction=REFINE","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Participatory Information Technology","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lea Gulstav","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","name":"Dalgaard, Lea Gulstav","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"b600b501-1612-47fd-9286-f687efaefaf0","name":"Grönvall, Erik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nervo","key":"verdezotopau","last":"Verdezoto","locid":"ce629209-5619-4b43-88fb-b8fd03725adb","name":"Verdezoto, Nervo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Venet","key":"osmanpedh","last":"Osman","name":"Osman, Venet","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrew","key":"campbellpedh","last":"Campbell","name":"Campbell, Andrew","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul","key":"lukowiczpedh","last":"Lukowicz","name":"Lukowicz, Paul","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4108/pervasivehealth.2013.252058","eisbn":["9781936968800"],"isbn":["9781479902965"],"pages":"137-144","place":"Venice, Italy","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"The 7th International Conference on Pervasive Computing Technologies for Healthcare"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84883112744"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f5fb8d89-1705-4f20-a9b4-e56383f8bd0e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Accounting for Medication Particularities: Designing for Everyday Medication Management","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-269664","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Objectives The present study aims to augment the network of home care around elderly. We investigate the nature of cooperative work between relatives and home care workers around elderly persons; present the CareCoor system developed to support that work; and report experiences from two pilot tests of CareCoor. Methods We employed ethnographic fieldwork methods and conducted participatory design workshops to throw light on the nature of cooperative home care work, and to elicit implications for the design of an IT system that would support the work of relatives and home care workers around elderly persons. The design implications led to the development of a prototype, called CareCoor, which is accessible via a tablet PC and on the Internet. CareCoor was subsequently evaluated in two pilot tests. The first lasted a week and included three elderly, their next of kin and the affiliated home care workers, while the second test lasted for six weeks and involved five elderly people, their next of kin and relevant home care workers. Results In the paper we make three major points, namely, (1) home care work is highly cooperative in nature and involves substantial coordinative efforts on the part of the actors involved, (2) the network of care around elderly can be augmented with new technology that allows all members of the network to follow, influence and be a part of the cooperative care of the elderly, and (3) CareCoor, the prototype introduced in this study, shows promise as it was well received during test and evaluation. Conclusion Home care work is increasingly important due to the ageing populations of Europe, the USA and large parts of Asia. Home care work between relatives and home care workers is inherently a cooperative effort, and can be facilitated and augmented by new information technology such as CareCoor. The pilot tests of CareCoor revealed promising results and will be further developed and evaluated in a larger test.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bossen, Claus","Christensen, Lars Rune","Grönvall, Erik","Vestergaard, Lasse"],"cuid":["S03-095.38-002318"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Computer Supported Cooperative Work","Coordination","Health care","Home care work","IT design","Peace of mind","Pårørende","Reciprocity","Sundheds IT","Tablet PC","Workplace study","ældre"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"carecoor augmenting the coordination of cooperative home care work","src":["aau","au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijmedinf.2012.10.005","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-095.38-002318","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000318998000012","type":"wos"},{"id":"23127539","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84876987749","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2e2e741d-ea7d-4327-a958-3e68bdbd3f45","au-e1a1b4cb-0d3a-415b-b844-0216ef7e68b3","itu-97bf6a62-e5ff-471c-9c7f-62b76c15465b"],"keyword":["Coordination","Hjemmeservice","IT design","Koordinations-arbejde","Peace of mind","Reciprocity","Sundheds It","Tablet PC","Workplace study","computer supported cooperative work","health care","home care work","pårørende","ældre"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-82090EF5BA5C72A13848A2ED21E91B8C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com.ez.statsbiblioteket.dk:2048/science/article/pii/S1386505612001979","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijmedinf.2012.10.005","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Information Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Institut for Æstetik og Kommunikation - Informationsvidenskab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, The Techno-Anthropology Research Group (Learning)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Center for Design, Innovation and Sustainable Transitions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The De