":"67-70","publisher":"global-interaction.org","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 3rd International Workshop","title":"Infrastructures for Healthcare:"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-68483660-25cf-4554-8b84-b66623db0562"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Augmented Binder-Supporting Cooperative Home Care Work","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-188915","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Percentage of Vestibular Dysfunction in 361 Elderly Citizens Responding to a Newspaper Advertisement. Brandt M, Grönvall E, Henriksen JJ, Larsen SB, Læssøe U, Mørch MM, Damsgaard EM Introduction Elderly patients with vestibular dysfunction have an eight-fold increased risk of falling compared to other fall patients. We believe that elderly patients with vestibular dysfunction either don’t consult their GP or have been abandoned by their GP. The aim of this study was to identify the percentage of vestibular dysfunction among elderly citizens with complaints of dizziness responding to a newspaper advertisement. Method To recruit elderly citizens with dizziness we advertised in a local newspaper. A telephone interview with the respondents was done by a physiotherapist (PT). If the PT concluded that the reason for the dizziness could be vestibular dysfunction the citizen was invited to further examinations. The citizen was tested by the PT and a nurse in the Fall Clinic, Department of Geriatrics, Aarhus University Hospital. If the patient was still under suspicion of vestibular dysfunction he/she was examined by a geriatrician and eventually by a specially trained otoneurologist on the ENT Department, Aarhus University Hospital. Results 361 elderly citizens responded to the advertisement. 8 patients had alcohol problems, 14 had significantly impaired vision, 42 had evidence of orthostatic hypotension, 49 didn’t want to participate, 50 had evidence of Benign Paroxysmal Positional Vertigo (BPPV), and 74 had disequilibrium without dizziness. 124 patients were suspected of vestibular dysfunction and further tested in the Fall Clinic. 71 of these patients have been seen until now and in 37 (52 %) vestibular dysfunction were diagnosed. BPPV was diagnosed in 21 (30%) of the patients having vestibular dysfunction. Of 37 patients having vestibular dysfunction, 16 needed further testing in the ENT Department. BPPV was diagnosed in further 4 patients. Conclusions Vestibular dysfunction among the elderly is an overlooked problem and may be relatively simply diagnosed by vestibular bedside tests. In this study surprisingly many citizens had BPPV, which can be diagnosed by the Epley maneuver or the Roll test.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Smærup, Michael","Læssøe, Uffe","Damsgaard, Else Marie","Grönvall, Erik","Larsen, Simon"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-049907"],"event":{"end":"2011-09-30","place":"Malaga, es","start":"2011-09-28","title":"7th Congress of the EUGMS 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-DTU","DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"percentage of vestibular dysfunction in 000000000361 elderly citizens responding to a newspaper advertisement","src":["ucn","via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-100.00-049907","ids":["ucn-4a42fbaa-be7f-45e3-bc51-2cf786e9b68a","via-4a42fbaa-be7f-45e3-bc51-2cf786e9b68a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-2-EF19E38036A962F9290D9ACAE80D268B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Uddannelser, Sundhedsuddannelserne"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus Univeristy Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Danmarks Tekniske Universitet"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Instituttet A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"smæruppau","last":"Smærup","locid":"20a14cf3-19ee-4f2d-8571-2a4e5af646db","name":"Smærup, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Uffe","key":"læssøepau","last":"Læssøe","locid":"f2c779f7-db32-43f5-8856-c9708e0a90aa","name":"Læssøe, Uffe","orcid":"0000-0001-5388-1671","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Else Marie","key":"damsgaardpau","last":"Damsgaard","name":"Damsgaard, Else Marie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","name":"Grönvall, Erik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Simon","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","GTS Institutes","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-4a42fbaa-be7f-45e3-bc51-2cf786e9b68a","via-4a42fbaa-be7f-45e3-bc51-2cf786e9b68a"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark","VIA University College"],"title":"Percentage of vestibular dysfunction in 361 elderly citizens responding to a newspaper advertisement","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-049907","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The Western welfare model is under pressure and finding new ways of providing care is a key issue to maintain a reasonable service level for elderly people spending their last years at a nursing home. Personal care at nursing homes tends to (quite reasonably) have high priority at the expense of social activities, thus creating situations where a number of elderly people experience loneliness. This paper presents ongoing work that focuses on developing Information and Communication Technology (ICT) for nursing homes that brings together professional care activities and family initiated care. We discuss challenges and opportunities for welfare or assistive technology design to support articulation work in a care setting, where both care professionals and family members (of the elderly inhabitants) co-exists. Furthermore, the care sector at hand suffers from economical limitations that challenge a successful implementation of more costly technologies. We present a concept named Care to Share? that seeks to bring together professional and family initiated care and that assists in the articulation work of social activities in a nursing home.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Asboe, Mark","Grönvall, Erik","Lassen, Henry Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-253968"],"event":{"end":"2011-05-23","place":"Dublin, ie","start":"2011-05-23","title":"2nd International Workshop on User Centered Design of Pervasive Healthcare Applications 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"care to share social innovation through low budget high impact welfare technologies","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/80054939956","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-253968","identifier":[{"id":"80054939956","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-da52916d-06eb-4373-ba19-dc3d6355e316"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A0D272002451F323B4F11A2408388E92"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"asboepau","last":"Asboe","locid":"325e1507-123e-40ae-9346-4213248ac016","name":"Asboe, Mark","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"b600b501-1612-47fd-9286-f687efaefaf0","name":"Grönvall, Erik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henry Michael","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"d658f81d-5ddb-4a54-a002-c4d4af481a87","name":"Lassen, Henry Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781612847672"],"pages":"568-571","publisher":"IEEE Computer Society Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 5th International Conference on Pervasive Computing Technologies for Healthcare"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-da52916d-06eb-4373-ba19-dc3d6355e316"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Care to Share? Social innovation through low-budget, high impact welfare technologies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-253968","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The project described in this paper aims to provide assistive tools to support elderly people affected by vestibular dysfunction (i.e. a form of balance disorder leading to dizziness and nausea) in their home-based rehabilitation activities. Challenges emerge as the rehabilitation moves from a supervised hospital setting to private homes. Our studies have shown that the elderly people are less motivated to perform the training at home. This paper presents a tangible, portable, two dimensional modular platform called LinkLights that has been developed to sustain the home-based rehabilitation, giving clear guidelines what to do, adding motivational cues and elements of variation and surprise in the activity. Furthermore, a set of challenges for successful translocation of the therapeutic regimen from a supervised, hospital setting to an unsupervised home-based setting together with some early results of experimenting with this platform will be presented.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grönvall, Erik","Kramp, Gunnar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-228956"],"event":{"end":"2011-05-27","place":"Kreta, gr","start":"2011-05-25","title":"4th International Conference on Pervasive Technologies Related to Assistive Environments 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"linklights a modular user adaptable system to support rehabilitation practices","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2141622.2141626","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-228956","ids":["au-aea3d44c-b85c-4d20-b8eb-6727423530af"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-1F53AB4DBDE1B2DF6CCA2975ACB3CD61"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2141622.2141626","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"b600b501-1612-47fd-9286-f687efaefaf0","name":"Grönvall, Erik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gunnar","key":"kramppau","last":"Kramp","locid":"ddcf0306-e2a9-4b7c-8b6a-475a022fbc7a","name":"Kramp, Gunnar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2141622.2141626","isbn":["9781450307727"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 4th International Conference on PErvasive Technologies Related to Assistive Environments"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84858012680"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-aea3d44c-b85c-4d20-b8eb-6727423530af"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"LinkLights : a modular, user adaptable system to support rehabilitation practices","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-228956","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Christensen, Lars Rune","Grönvall, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383020"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the augmented binder supporting cooperative home care work","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383020","ids":["itu-76e444fa-9ceb-4143-8053-350faf0b7d51"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F08587CC404A08D2F14B4C960217FB26"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"gronvallpau","last":"Gronvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","name_org":"Gronvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 3rd International Workshop Infrastructures in Healthcare, IT- University, Copenhagen, 23rd June – 24 June. 2011."},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-76e444fa-9ceb-4143-8053-350faf0b7d51"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Augmented Binder: Supporting Cooperative Home Care Work. ","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383020","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Table of Contents Motivation -- Participatory Design (PD) activities in private homes challenge how we relate to the PD process, compared to PD in professional settings. Grounded in a project related to chronic dizziness among older people, we outline four challenges. These challenges, we argue, have to be carefully addressed when PD processes include the home. Research approach -- A PD project developing rehabilitation technologies for elderly people in private homes has been used to reflect on home-based PD projects compared with more traditional, workplace-oriented PD projects such as Utopia. Findings -- We identify four challenges in home-based PD. The challenges are 1) Negotiating knowledge about the home, 2) Ill, weak users, 3) Divergent interests of participants and 4) Usable and sustainable post-project solutions. These challenges are used to reflect upon differences between a home-based PD process, such as ours with non-workers, and work-place projects, such as Utopia. Through this reflection, the paper contributes to a more general discussion on PD in non-work settings with weak users. Research limitations -- The paper is grounded in one project where the elderly participants are heavily affected by their illness. Furthermore, they have no or very little experience with ICT, e.g. computers or mobile phones. Take away message -- Differences do exist between traditional PD projects in work settings, such as Utopia, and home-based PD with weak users especially in relation to knowledge about settings and how to reconcile differences in interests. The home as a place for (technology-assisted) treatment and PD must be carefully analyzed, and diverse interests and roles should be negotiated among all stakeholders.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grönvall, Erik","Kyng, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-137094"],"event":{"end":"2011-08-26","place":"Rostock, de","start":"2011-08-24","title":"European Conference on Cognitive Ergonomics. ECCE 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beyond utopia reflections on participatory design in home based healthcare with weak users","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2074712.2074750","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-137094","identifier":[{"id":"84255176462","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0d8b5711-0cf2-4d27-b22c-e8426893be2d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-570B29F67DF812D3E7ABD086945453D0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2074712.2074750","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"b600b501-1612-47fd-9286-f687efaefaf0","name":"Grönvall, Erik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"kyngpau","last":"Kyng","locid":"f0486b10-a937-4cd9-aa99-168060eea4fc","name":"Kyng, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2074712.2074750","isbn":["9781450310291"],"pages":"189-196","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 29th Annual European Conference on Cognitive Ergonomics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84255176462"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0d8b5711-0cf2-4d27-b22c-e8426893be2d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Beyond Utopia : Reflections on Participatory Design in home-based healthcare with weak users","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-137094","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
